# Confluence adapter: reading and writing Confluence pages
error-conf-action-key-used = That change has already been sent to Confluence. Nothing more to do.
error-conf-approval-failed = The approval for that change was refused. Ask for approval again.
error-conf-conversion-failed = The page content couldn't be converted for Confluence. Check it and try again.
error-conf-datastore-unavailable = ordin can't reach its saved work just now. Try again in a moment.
error-conf-files-failed = ordin couldn't read or save a file while syncing. Try again.
error-conf-link-not-active = That Confluence link isn't active. Reconnect it and try again.
error-conf-location-invalid = The saved Confluence location isn't valid. Link the page again.
error-conf-not-tracked = ordin isn't tracking changes for that link yet. Sync it first.
error-conf-origin-changed = The Confluence page changed after you read it. Bring in the latest version and try again.
error-conf-outcome-unknown = The Confluence change took too long and may have gone through. Check the page before trying again.
error-conf-response-invalid = Confluence sent back something ordin couldn't read. Try again in a moment.
error-conf-site-not-granted = Your Confluence sign-in can't reach your company's site. Sign in to Confluence again.
error-conf-title-exists = A page with that title already exists in the space. Choose another title.
error-conf-too-large = That page or attachment is too big for Confluence. Make it smaller and try again.
